# STANDARD: SECURITY

## Context

- **When:** Writing API routes, database queries, forms, user input handling
- **Goal:** Prevent OWASP Top 10 vulnerabilities in generated code
- **Impact:** CRM system handles customer data — security is critical

---

## Requirements

### Input Validation (ALL API routes)

<required>
  - Every route handler MUST validate request body/params/query with Zod
  - Validate BEFORE any business logic
  - Return 400 with validation errors, not 500
</required>

```typescript
// GOOD: Zod validation at route level
const schema = z.object({ id: z.number().positive(), name: z.string().min(1) });
router.post('/endpoint', async (req, res) => {
  const result = schema.safeParse(req.body);
  if (!result.success) return res.status(400).json({ errors: result.error.issues });
  // proceed with result.data
});
```

### SQL Injection Prevention

<critical>
  - ALWAYS use parameterized queries ($1, $2, ...)
  - NEVER concatenate user input into SQL strings
  - NEVER use template literals for SQL with user data
</critical>

```typescript
// GOOD: Parameterized
await pool.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1', [userId]);

// BAD: String concatenation — SQL INJECTION RISK
await pool.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${userId}`);
```

### XSS Prevention

<required>
  - Never use dangerouslySetInnerHTML with user data
  - Escape HTML entities when rendering user-provided text
  - Sanitize data at API boundary, not just display
</required>

### Authentication & Authorization

<required>
  - Check auth middleware on every protected route
  - Verify user has permission for the specific resource
  - Never trust client-side data for authorization decisions
</required>

### Common Anti-patterns (FORBIDDEN)

| Pattern | Risk | Fix |
|---------|------|-----|
| `eval(userInput)` | Remote Code Execution | Never use eval with user data |
| `innerHTML = userText` | XSS | Use textContent or sanitize |
| `` `SELECT ... ${var}` `` | SQL Injection | Parameterized queries |
| Logging passwords/tokens | Data leak | Never log sensitive data |
| Hardcoded secrets in code | Credential exposure | Use env vars / .secrets/ |

---

## Quick Check

```markdown
## Security Check
- [ ] All route inputs validated with Zod
- [ ] All SQL queries parameterized
- [ ] No user data in innerHTML/dangerouslySetInnerHTML
- [ ] Auth middleware on protected routes
- [ ] No secrets hardcoded in code
- [ ] No sensitive data in logs
```

